 {"id":"fabro-93f2","title":"gofib: add -step <int> flag printing every step-th number of the selected range","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:03:56.493Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:13:17.542Z","description":"Today gofib prints every Fibonacci number in the selected range (-n/-start/-limit). Add a -step flag (default 1) that strides the selection: with -step k, only every k-th number of the selected range prints, in every output mode (text, json, pretty, table, csv).\n\nRules: -step must be >= 1 (invalid values exit non-zero with a stderr message naming the flag and the rule, like -n); -step 1 behaves exactly as today; a positive -seed keeps single-index semantics and ignores -step (not an error); -sum sums the numbers that remain AFTER stepping.\n\nAcceptance: (1) gofib -n 6 -step 2 prints 3 numbers (first, third, fifth of the six); (2) -step 0 and -step -2 exit non-zero with a stderr line naming the flag; (3) -step 2 -json emits JSON Lines with exactly the stepped indices; (4) unit tests cover stride selection, validation errors, and the -seed interaction; (5) just qualitygate stays green.","closedAt":"2026-09-03T21:13:17.542Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-87cf","title":"gofib: add -last <int> flag printing only the last k numbers of the selected range","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:03:56.580Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:18:25.491Z","description":"Add -last k (default 0 = unset) to print only the LAST k numbers of the selected range, in every output mode.\n\nRules: k must be >= 1 when set (invalid values exit non-zero with a stderr message naming the flag); if the selection has fewer than k numbers, print all of them (clamp, not an error); combination order is selection (-n/-start/-limit) then -step stride then -last tail (document the order in the flag help text); a positive -seed overrides everything single-index style and conflicts with -last like it conflicts with -sum (exit non-zero, stderr names both flags).\n\nAcceptance: (1) gofib -n 10 -last 3 prints the 3 highest indices of the default sequence; (2) gofib -n 2 -last 5 prints both numbers (clamp); (3) -last 0 behaves as today; (4) -last -1 exits non-zero with stderr naming the flag; (5) -last 2 -step 2 takes the last 2 of the stepped selection; (6) unit tests cover tail selection, clamping, validation, ordering with -step, and the -seed conflict; (7) just qualitygate stays green.","closedAt":"2026-09-03T21:18:25.491Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-2652","title":"engine: refresh the goal line per seed cycle or stamp the seed id into the run header","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:24:38.152Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:24:50.085Z","description":"Painpoint from run 01M1MHGS7PH26EP20B2RTAPN4G (reviewer@2): the run goal text goes stale relative to the pipeline — it names fabro-93f2 (-step) while the in-progress seed, spec, evidence, and closeout had moved on to fabro-87cf (-last). The reviewer had to reconcile manually and trust the evidence capture spec as authoritative. Fix directions: refresh the goal line per cycle, or stamp the active seed id into the goal/header the context pipeline renders (the seed trio keys are already authoritative — the goal is display text). Filed from the stage journal per the painpoint channel.","closedAt":"2026-09-03T21:24:50.085Z","closeReason":"Filed on the wrong tracker (lab); moved to the platform tracker on denkhaus — engine behavior, not fib product work."}
-{"id":"fabro-1f5b","title":"gofib tests: replace per-flag opts() wrappers with one options-literal builder","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:49:50.514Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:49:50.514Z","description":"From run 01M1MHGS7PH26EP20B2RTAPN4G (implementer@3 observation): fib_test.go predates the newer flags (-step, -last); every flag combination needed its own opts wrapper (stepOpts, lastOpts, ...), and each future flag would add another. Composing flags in tests drifts toward wrapper soup.\n\nRefactor: ONE test helper that takes an options literal (or builder) defaulting to the current defaults (n=100, start=0, limit=0, seed=0, step=1, last=0, format unset, json/pretty/sum/version false, output empty) and overrides only what a test exercises. All existing tests migrate to it; the per-flag wrappers are deleted.\n\nAcceptance: (1) exactly ONE options-construction helper remains in fib_test.go; (2) no test constructs options{} literals inline except through the helper; (3) behavior-neutral — the full test suite passes unchanged assertions; (4) just qualitygate stays green."}
